Gate native semantic diagnostics on build data / proc-macros having been
fetched, not on them being missing.

The upstream condition asserts `last_op_result().is_none()`, which is the
inverse of the intent documented right above it ("have finished fetching the
build data once"). With `cargo.buildScripts.enable` or `procMacro.enable` on
(the defaults, and what config.yaml ships), `fetch_semantic` flips to false as
soon as the first build-data/proc-macro fetch completes, so rust-analyzer only
ever publishes syntax diagnostics and type errors never reach the editor.

Upstream as of 2026-08-10.1 still carries the bug; drop this patch once it is
fixed upstream.
